  note:{h:"Blame-free language",html:`<p>In English business culture, describe <b>the problem</b>, not <b>the person</b>.</p><table><tr><th>Sounds like blame</th><th>Better</th></tr><tr><td>Marek made a mistake in the order.</td><td>There was a mistake in the order.</td></tr><tr><td>You didn't send the file.</td><td>It seems the file wasn't sent.</td></tr><tr><td>IT broke the system.</td><td>The system stopped working after the update.</td></tr></table><p class="ok">✓ <b>due to</b> + noun: due to bad weather · <b>because</b> + sentence: because the truck broke down</p><p class="no">✗ due to the truck broke down</p>`},
