  note:{h:"First conditional and 'will' for promises",html:`<table><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td><b>If</b> + present, <b>will</b> + verb</td><td>If we <b>rent</b> a truck, we<b>'ll deliver</b> on time.</td></tr><tr><td><b>I'll</b> + verb (offer / promise)</td><td>I<b>'ll call</b> the supplier this afternoon.</td></tr></table><p class="no">✗ If we will rent a truck, we deliver on time.</p><p class="no">✗ I call the supplier. (when you offer)</p><div class="bz-box tip">Every decision needs <b>three things</b>: what, who, and by when.</div>`},
